<h1>INTRODUCTION</h1>
<h2>How This Book Came to Be</h2>

<p>
	In the early summer of 2004, I <strong>got a phone call</strong> from Steve
	Jobs. He had been <strong>scattershot</strong> friendly to me over the years,
	with occasional <strong>bursts of intensity</strong>, especially when he was
	<strong>launching</strong> a new product that he wanted on the cover of
	<em>Time</em> or <strong>featured</strong> on CNN, places where I’d worked.
	But now that I was no longer at either of those places, I hadn’t
	<strong>heard from</strong> him much. We talked a bit about the Aspen
	Institute, which I had recently joined, and I invited him to speak at our
	summer campus in Colorado. He’d be happy to come, he said, but not to be
	<strong>onstage</strong>. He wanted instead to <strong>take a walk</strong> so
	that we could talk.
