	<strong>biography</strong> of him. I had recently published one on Benjamin
	Franklin and was writing one about Albert Einstein, and my initial reaction
	was to wonder, <strong>half jokingly</strong>, whether he saw himself as the
	natural <strong>successor</strong> in that sequence. Because I assumed that he
	was still <strong>in the middle of</strong> an
	<strong>oscillating</strong> career that had many more
	<strong>ups and downs</strong> left, I <strong>demurred</strong>. Not now, I
