	розыгрыши, как и ты, и тоже увлекается созданием электронной техники».
</p>

<p>
	It may have been the most significant meeting in a Silicon Valley garage since
	Hewlett <strong>went into</strong> Packard’s thirty-two years earlier. “Steve and I just sat on
	the sidewalk in front of Bill’s house <strong>for the longest time</strong>, just sharing
	stories—mostly about <strong>pranks we’d pulled</strong>, and also what kind of electronic
	designs we’d done,” Wozniak recalled. “We had so much in common.”
</p>
