	народу».
</p>

<p>
	There were occasional Wednesday-night <strong>potluck dinners</strong>, and
	two of the <strong>regulars</strong>, Gordon French and Fred Moore, decided to create a more
	formal club where news about personal electronics could be shared. They were
	energized by the arrival of the January 1975 issue of
	<strong>Popular Mechanics</strong>, which had on its cover the first personal
	<strong>computer kit</strong>, the Altair.
</p>
