	комплект для сборки персонального компьютера — Altair.
</p>

<p>
	The Altair <strong>wasn’t much</strong>—just a $495 <strong>pile of parts</strong> that had to be soldered to a
	board that would then do little—but for hobbyists and hackers it
	<strong>heralded</strong> the dawn of a new era. Bill Gates and Paul Allen
	read the magazine and started working on a version of BASIC, an easy-to-use
	programming language, for the Altair.
</p>
