</p>

<p>
	Moore wrote the <strong>flyer</strong> for the first meeting, held on March 5, 1975, in
	French’s Menlo Park garage: “Are you building your own computer? Terminal, TV,
	typewriter?” it asked. “If so, you might like to come to a <strong>gathering</strong> of people
	with <strong>like-minded</strong> interests.”
</p>
<table class="explanation">
	<tr>
		<td><strong>flyer</strong></td>
		<td>листовка, объявление</td>
	</tr>
	<tr>
		<td><strong>like-minded</strong></td>
