	детали», — вспоминал Джобс.
</p>

<p>
	“So the fifty we sold to the Byte Shop almost paid for all the material we
	needed to make a hundred boards.” Now they could make a real profit by selling
	the <strong>remaining</strong> fifty to their friends and Homebrew
	<strong>compatriots</strong>. Elizabeth Holmes officially became the <strong>part-time</strong>
	bookkeeper at $4 an hour, driving down from San Francisco once a week and
	figuring out how to <strong>port</strong> Jobs’s checkbook into a <strong>ledger</strong>.
