</p>

<p>
	Not surprisingly, they had <strong>contradictory impulses</strong>: Wozniak wanted to sell them
	for about what it cost to build them, but Jobs wanted to make a serious
	profit. Jobs <strong>prevailed</strong>. He picked a <strong>retail price</strong> that was about three times
