	комнате», — предполагал Коттке.
</p>

<p>
	Even though her relationship with Jobs was <strong>sporadic</strong>, Brennan
	soon moved in as well. This made for a set of living arrangements
	<strong>worthy of</strong> a French farce. The house had two big bedrooms and
	two tiny ones. Jobs, not surprisingly, <strong>commandeered</strong> the
	largest of them, and Brennan (who was not really living with him) moved into
	the other big bedroom.
</p>
