	wanted to marry, and we would never be happy, and it wouldn’t last long,” Jobs
	later said. “I was <strong>all in favor of</strong> her getting an abortion,
	but she didn’t know what to do. She thought about it repeatedly and decided
	not to, or I don’t know that she ever really decided—I think time just decided
	for her.” Brennan told me that it was her choice to have the baby: “He said he
	was fine with an abortion but never <strong>pushed for</strong> it.”
	Interestingly, given his own background, he was adamantly against one option.
	“He strongly <strong>discouraged</strong> me putting the child up for
	adoption,” she said.
</p>
