	Годы спустя Джобс раскаивался в своём поведении — один из немногих случаев,
	когда он это признавал:
</p>

<p>
	I wish I had <strong>handled</strong> it differently. I could not see myself
	as a father then, so I didn’t <strong>face up to</strong> it. But when the
	test results showed she was my daughter, it’s not true that I doubted it. I
	agreed to support her until she was eighteen and give some money to Chrisann
	as well. I found a house in Palo Alto and <strong>fixed it up</strong> and let
	them live there <strong>rent-free</strong>. Her mother found her great schools
	which I paid for. I tried to do the right thing. But if I could
	<strong>do it over</strong>, I would do a better job.
</p>
