	Барбара Ясински.
</p>

<p>
	There was still, <strong>to be sure</strong>, a childlike
	<strong>rebellious streak</strong> in him. He, Jasinski, and Kottke liked to
	go <strong>skinny-dipping</strong> in Felt Lake on the edge of Interstate 280
	near Stanford, and he bought a 1966 BMW R60/2 motorcycle that he
	<strong>adorned</strong> with orange <strong>tassels</strong> on the
	handlebars. He could also still be bratty. He
	<strong>belittled</strong> waitresses and frequently returned food with the
	proclamation that it was “garbage.” At the company’s first Halloween party, in
	1979, he dressed in robes as Jesus Christ, an act of semi-ironic
	self-awareness that he considered funny but that caused a lot of
	<strong>eye rolling</strong>.
</p>
