</p>

<p>
	Even his initial <strong>stirrings of domesticity</strong> had some quirks. He
	bought a proper house in the Los Gatos hills, which he
	<strong>adorned</strong> with a Maxfield Parrish painting, a Braun
	coffeemaker, and Henckels knives. But because he was so
	<strong>obsessive</strong> when it came to selecting
	<strong>furnishings</strong>, it remained mostly <strong>barren</strong>,
	lacking beds or chairs or couches. Instead his bedroom had a mattress in the
	center, framed pictures of Einstein and Maharaj-ji on the walls, and an Apple
	II on the floor.
</p>
