	some unnecessary step, such as handing over the credit card or printing a
	receipt. “If you look at the stores and the products, you will see Steve’s
	obsession with beauty as simplicity—this Bauhaus aesthetic and wonderful
	minimalism, which goes all the way to the checkout process in the stores,”
	said Ellison. “It means the absolute minimum number of steps. Steve gave us
	<strong>the exact, explicit recipe</strong> for how he wanted the checkout to work.”
