	able to walk into a retail space and, <strong>with one sweep of the eye</strong>, understand
	the flow. Jobs agreed that simplicity and lack of distractions were keys to a
	great store, as they were to a product. “After that, <strong>he nailed it</strong>,” said
	Drexler. “The vision he had was complete control of the entire experience of
	his product, from how it was designed and made to how it was sold.”
</p>
