	нас один».
</p>

<p>
	Jobs liked to tell the story—and he did so to his team that day—about how
	everything that he had done correctly had required a moment when he <strong>hit the
	rewind button</strong>. In each case he had to <strong>rework</strong> something that he discovered was
	not perfect. He talked about doing it on
	<strong>Toy Story</strong>, when the character of Woody had evolved into being
	<strong>a jerk</strong>, and on a couple of occasions with the original Macintosh. “If
	something isn’t right, you can’t just ignore it and say you’ll fix it later,”
	he said. “That’s what other companies do.”
</p>
