<p class="translation">
	Поэтому с 1999 года Apple начала выпускать приложения для Mac — с расчётом на
	людей на стыке искусства и технологии. Среди них: Final Cut Pro для монтажа
	цифрового видео; iMovie — попроще, для потребителей; iDVD — для записи видео
	или музыки на диск; iPhoto — конкурент Adobe Photoshop; GarageBand — для
	создания и сведения музыки; iTunes — для управления песнями; и iTunes Store —
	для их покупки.
</p>

<p>
	The idea of the digital hub quickly came into focus. “I first understood this
	with the camcorder,” Jobs said. “Using iMovie makes your camcorder ten times
	more valuable.” Instead of having hundreds of hours of
	<strong>raw footage</strong> you would never really
	<strong>sit through</strong>, you could edit it on your computer, make elegant
	<strong>dissolves</strong>, add music, and <strong>roll credits</strong>,
	listing yourself as executive producer. It allowed people to be creative, to
	express themselves, to make something emotional. “That’s when it
	<strong>hit me</strong> that the personal computer was going to
	<strong>morph into</strong> something else.”
</p>
