</p>

<p>
	Initially there was some skepticism among tech geeks, especially about the
	$399 price. In <strong>the blogosphere</strong>, the joke was that iPod stood
	for “idiots price our devices.” However, consumers soon made it a hit. More
	than that, the iPod became the essence of everything Apple was
	<strong>destined to be</strong>: poetry connected to engineering, arts and
	creativity intersecting with technology, design that’s bold and simple. It had
	an <strong>ease of use</strong> that came from being an integrated end-to-end
	system, from computer to FireWire to device to software to content management.
	When you took an iPod out of the box, it was so beautiful that it seemed to
	<strong>glow</strong>, and it made all other music players look as if they had
	been designed and manufactured in Uzbekistan.
</p>
