	шёл».
</p>

<p>
	He then jumped from <strong>the sublime</strong> to the sixties: Donovan’s “Catch the Wind.”
	When he noticed me <strong>look askance</strong>, he protested, “Donovan did some really good
	stuff, really.” He punched up “Mellow Yellow,” and then admitted that perhaps
	it was not the best example. “It sounded better when we were young.”
