	his suggestions, usually valuable and often brilliant, on ways to improve each
	movie project, theme park ride, <strong>television pilot</strong>, and countless other
	products. But after Wells was killed in a helicopter crash in 1994, Eisner
	never found the right manager. Katzenberg had demanded Wells’s job, which is
	why Eisner <strong>ousted him</strong>. Michael Ovitz became president in 1995; it was not a
	pretty sight, and he was gone in less than two years. Jobs later offered his
	assessment:
</p>
