<p>
	Jobs <strong>got panicky</strong>. He had always written his own presentations, but he had
	never done a commencement address. One night he sat down and wrote the speech
	himself, with no help other than <strong>bouncing ideas off his wife</strong>. As a result, it
	turned out to be a very intimate and simple talk, with the <strong>unadorned</strong> and
	personal feel of a perfect Steve Jobs product.
