	2005, after coming back from his cancer surgery, the surprise party that his
	wife arranged featured mainly his closest friends and professional colleagues.
	It was at the comfortable San Francisco home of some friends, and the great
	chef Alice Waters prepared salmon from Scotland along with <strong>couscous</strong> and a
	variety of garden-raised vegetables. “It was beautifully warm and intimate,
	with everyone and the kids all able to sit in one room,” Waters recalled. The
	entertainment was comedy <strong>improvisation</strong> done by the cast of
	<strong>Whose Line Is It Anyway?</strong>
	Jobs’s close friend Mike Slade was there, along with colleagues from Apple and
	Pixar, including Lasseter, Cook, Schiller, Clow, Rubinstein, and Tevanian.
</p>
