<p class="translation">
	Моссберг хотел, чтобы вечернее совместное выступление стало дружеской беседой,
	а не дебатами, — но шансы таяли, когда Джобс днём, в сольном интервью,
	проехался по Microsoft. На вопрос о чрезвычайной популярности iTunes для
	Windows он пошутил: «Это как подать стакан ледяной воды кому-то в аду».
</p>

<p>
	So when it was time for Gates and Jobs to meet in <strong>the green room</strong> before their
	joint session that evening, Mossberg was worried. Gates got there first, with
	his aide Larry Cohen, who had <strong>briefed him</strong> about Jobs’s remark earlier that
	day. When Jobs <strong>ambled in</strong> a few minutes later, he grabbed a bottle of water
	from the ice bucket and sat down. After a moment or two of silence, Gates
	said, “So I guess I’m the representative from hell.” He wasn’t smiling. Jobs
	paused, gave him one of his <strong>impish grins</strong>, and handed him the ice water. Gates
	relaxed, and <strong>the tension dissipated</strong>.
</p>
