	market, the integrated approach, as manifested in his iTunes-iPod package, was
	proving to be the better, he noted, but Microsoft’s <strong>decoupled approach</strong> was
	<strong>faring better</strong> in the personal computer market. One question he raised in an
	offhand way was: Which approach might work better for mobile phones?
</p>
