	регулярно и докладывал о новых продуктах. «Он светлел каждый раз, стоило
	разговору повернуть на Apple, — говорил Кук. — Будто включали свет». Компанию
	он любил глубоко и, казалось, жил перспективой возвращения. Детали заряжали
	его. Когда Кук описывал новую модель iPhone, Джобс следующий час обсуждал не
	только название — сошлись на iPhone 3GS, — но и размер и шрифт «GS»: должны ли
	буквы быть прописными (да) и курсивными (нет).
</p>

<p>
	One day Riley arranged a surprise after-hours visit to Sun Studio, the
	redbrick <strong>shrine</strong> where Elvis, Johnny Cash, B.B. King, and many other
	rock-and-roll pioneers recorded. They were given a private tour and a history
	lecture by one of the young staffers, who sat with Jobs on the
	cigarette-scarred bench that Jerry Lee Lewis used. Jobs was arguably the most
	influential person in the music industry at the time, but the kid didn’t
	recognize him <strong>in his emaciated state</strong>. As they were leaving, Jobs told Riley,
	“That kid was really smart. We should hire him for iTunes.” So Riley called
	Eddy Cue, who flew the boy out to California for an interview and ended up
	hiring him to help build the early R&amp;B and rock-and-roll sections of
	iTunes. When Riley went back to see his friends at Sun Studio later, they said
	that it proved, as their slogan said, that your dreams can still come true at
	Sun Studio.
</p>
