	пожаловался на статьи, утверждавшие, что инновации Apple зависят от Джобса и
	исчезнут, если он не вернётся. «Мне правда больно», — сказал Айв. Он
	чувствовал себя «опустошённым» и недооценённым.
</p>

<p>
	Jobs was likewise in a dark mental state after his return to Palo Alto. He was
	<strong>coming to grips with</strong> the thought that he might <strong>not</strong>
	be <strong>indispensable</strong> to the company. Apple stock had <strong>fared well</strong> while he was away,
	going from $82 when he announced his leave in January 2009 to $140 when he
	returned at the end of May. On one conference call with analysts shortly after
	Jobs went on leave, Cook departed from his unemotional style to give <strong>a rousing
	declaration</strong> of why Apple would continue to <strong>soar</strong> even with Jobs absent:
