	architecture, but it also bought a 150-person microprocessor design firm in
	Palo Alto, called P.A. Semi, and had it create a custom <strong>system-on-a-chip</strong>,
	called the A4, which was based on the ARM architecture and <strong>manufactured</strong> in
	South Korea by Samsung. As Jobs recalled:
