	software developers while <strong>retaining enough control</strong> to protect the <strong>integrity</strong> of
	the iPhone and the simplicity of the <strong>customer experience</strong>. “It was an
	absolutely magical solution that hit the <strong>sweet spot</strong>,” said Levinson. “It gave
	us the benefits of openness while retaining <strong>end-to-end control</strong>.”
