	whole <strong>subscription base</strong> to become subscribers of yours, for you to then
	aggregate at the Apple store,” said Bewkes. “And the next thing you’ll do,
	once you have a monopoly, is come back and tell me that my magazine shouldn’t
	be $4 a copy but instead should be $1. If someone subscribes to our magazine,
	we need to know who it is, we need to be able to create online communities of
	those people, and we need the right to <strong>pitch them directly</strong> about <strong>renewing</strong>.”
</p>

