	with Apple Corps, the <strong>holding company</strong> of the Beatles, which had first <strong>sued</strong> the
	<strong>fledgling</strong> computer company over use of the name in 1978. But that still did
	not get the Beatles into the iTunes Store. The band was the last major
	<strong>holdout</strong>, primarily because it had not <strong>resolved</strong> with EMI music, which owned
	most of its songs, how to handle the <strong>digital rights</strong>.
</p>

