<h1>CHAPTER FORTY</h1>
<h2><strong>TO INFINITY</strong></h2>
<h2>The Cloud, the Spaceship, and Beyond</h2>

<p><strong>The iPad 2</strong></p>
<p class="translation">iPad 2</p>

<p>
	Even before the iPad <strong>went on sale</strong>, Jobs was thinking about what should be in
	the iPad 2. It needed <strong>front and back cameras</strong>—everyone knew that was
	coming—and he definitely wanted it to be <strong>thinner</strong>. But there was a <strong>peripheral
	issue</strong> that he focused on that most people hadn’t thought about: The cases
	that people used covered the beautiful lines of the iPad and <strong>detracted from</strong>
	the screen. They made fatter what should be <strong>thinner</strong>. They put a <strong>pedestrian
	cloak</strong> on a device that should be <strong>magical in all of its aspects</strong>.
</p>

