	of your digital life. There was, however, a big problem: The service, to use
	Jobs’s terminology, <strong>sucked</strong>. It was complex, devices didn’t sync well, and
	email and other data <strong>got lost randomly in the ether</strong>. “Apple’s MobileMe Is
	Far Too <strong>Flawed</strong> to Be <strong>Reliable</strong>,” was the <strong>headline</strong> on Walt Mossberg’s <strong>review</strong>
