</p>

<p>
	The meeting actually lasted forty-five minutes, and Jobs <strong>did not hold back</strong>.
	“You’re <strong>headed for</strong> <strong>a one-term presidency</strong>,” Jobs told Obama <strong>at the outset</strong>. To
	prevent that, he said, the administration needed to be a lot more
	<strong>business-friendly</strong>. He described how easy it was to build a factory in China,
	and said that it was almost impossible to do so these days in America, largely
	because of <strong>regulations</strong> and <strong>unnecessary costs</strong>.
</p>

